	(text "LEPD LED driver + photodiode TIA: SPICE test bench (simulation only; nothing here is on the board).\nMirrors hardware/linear_cc_led_driver.kicad_sch channel 1, hardware/pd_amp.kicad_sch and hardware/tps7a4901.kicad_sch: same refs and values.\nDriver: +5V (V1, ideal buck) feeds the LED, U2 (MCP6242, DATASHEET STAND-IN), U3 (TI LM2901/LM339 model), Q1 (BC858 STAND-IN), Q2 (Infineon BSS806N_L1).\nChannel 1 (real refs) is driven by B1 = 5 V x duty (the PWM's average), duty = V4 (the swept x; 0 outside the DC sweep).\nCopies x200 / x300 / x400: the same channel driven by a 5 V PWM at 490.2 / 976.6 / 31372.5 Hz, 50 %.\nCopy x500: U502 + Q502 + RS501 driven straight by the step V8 (loop response). Copy x600: a 3.0 V LED (headroom), DC.\nRf R52 (10k, FEEDBACK -> INN) and Cf C36 (2.2n C0G, OPAMP_OUT -> INN) close the op-amp loop as on the board (R52-R55 / C36-C39);\nevery copy has its own (R252/C236 .. R652/C636), so x500 and the ac_loop_* / step_* measures show the compensated loop with the stand-in op-amp.\nLEDs are diode STAND-INS (models/standins.lib). V11, V211.. are 0 V ammeters in series with each LED. B2 / B602 output the FET dissipation in W.\nU7 (TPS7A4901) is an ideal error amplifier (STAND-IN) with VREF = V3 = 1.185 V, R49/R50/R51/C27/C28 as on the board; +5VA feeds U5, U6 and the bias dividers.\nTIA channel 1 (U5A, U6A, R33..R47) and channel 2 (U5B = U105, U6B = U106, R35..R48) have the photodiode as built:\ncathode on the summing node (J6.2/J7.2 = PD_CATHODE1/2 -> R37/R39 0R -> TIA_FEEDBACK_1/2), anode on TIA_BIAS_1/2 (J6.1/J7.1 = PD_ANODE1/2 -> R38/R40).\nR37-R40 (0R) are shorted. The DF2S6.8MFS TVS diodes D8, D12-D15 are left out:\nwith Toshiba's PSpice model (rev 1, not committed, licensed for simulation use) on D12-D15 the summing-node leakage is 4.4 pA at 27 C (+6.5 uV at TIA_OUT) and 0.17 nA at 85 C (+0.26 mV),\nand the 10.61 Hz TIA pole does not move. GNDA = GND here (no ground drops).\nEach photodiode: D106/D107 (dark junction + 11 pF, STAND-IN) and G106/G107, photocurrent = 3.2 uA x V4 from cathode to anode inside.\nU6 is TI's TLV914x model. PD1 / PD2 go to the Nano's A0 / A1.\nDF2S6.8MFS model, to repeat the TVS run (not committed: licensed for simulation use): Toshiba Electronic Devices & Storage, part DF2S6.8MFS,\nproduct page https://toshiba.semicon-storage.com/us/semiconductor/product/diodes/tvs-diodes-esd-protection-diodes/detail.DF2S6.8MFS.html.\nFiles as dropped: DF2S6.8MFS_PSpice_20250213.zip (DF2S6.8MFS_PSpice_rev1.lib) and\nDF2S6.8MFS_LTspice_20250828.zip (encrypted DF2S6.8MFS_LTspice_rev1_enc.lib + .asy). Use the PSpice lib: .include it, subckt DF2S6_8MFS (node 1 = device pin 2,\nnode 2 = device pin 1); per diode a 0 V ammeter and the part from the node to GND: VD12 /TIA_FEEDBACK_1 nD12 0 + XD12 0 nD12 DF2S6_8MFS, likewise D13\non /TIA_BIAS_1, D14 on /TIA_FEEDBACK_2, D15 on /TIA_BIAS_2; .options gmin=1e-12 rshunt=1e12; read i(vd12) on the DC and AC decks.\nResult: 4.36 pA out of the summing node at 27 C (+6.5 uV at TIA_OUT), 0.17 nA at 85 C (+0.26 mV, 0.05 LSB).\nChecks: expect.toml, run by check.py."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25.4 335.28 0)
